      "hints": [
        "Expand $(1 + x/2)^6 = 1 + 3x + \\frac{15}{4}x^2 + \\dots$",
        "Collect $x^2$ terms in $(4 + ax)(1 + 3x + \\frac{15}{4}x^2)$: $4\\left(\\frac{15}{4}\\right) + 3a = 3$.",
        "Solve for $a = -4$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Expand the first three terms of $\\left(1 + \\frac{x}{2}\\right)^6$ using the binomial theorem:\n$$\\left(1 + \\frac{x}{2}\\right)^6 = 1 + \\binom{6}{1}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) + \\binom{6}{2}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2 + \\dots = 1 + 3x + 15\\left(\\frac{x^2}{4}\\right) + \\dots = 1 + 3x + \\frac{15}{4}x^2 + \\dots$$",
        "Identify the terms producing $x^2$ in the product $(4 + ax)\\left(1 + 3x + \\frac{15}{4}x^2 + \\dots\\right)$:\n$$\\text{Term in } x^2 = 4\\left(\\frac{15}{4}x^2\\right) + ax(3x) = 15x^2 + 3ax^2 = (15 + 3a)x^2$$",
        "Equate the coefficient to $3$ and solve for $a$:\n$$15 + 3a = 3 \\implies 3a = 3 - 15 = -12 \\implies a = -4$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
